    T21
        title       Fragments and operations
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T20, @T9, @T12]
        description
            Build fragments, then operations with the required services list, and @spec.Reads, with the round-14
            carry list's unbuilt design items.

            **Why now:** the runtime cannot yet declare fragments or operations, or read resources, which
            the Reads area and the carry items judge.

            **Read first:** @spec.Reads, @spec.Compile.R9, @spec.Compile.R10, @spec.Compile.R11,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the round-14 carry list: the "design items not
            built" row).

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): name the Reads features
            that spec-split.md sets for "when the operations module reaches them", and write their Spec section first:
            staleTime and gcTime, trailing refetch, focus and connection triggers, holds, invalidate and clear, setData,
            write batches (256), optimistic stacking, placeholders and contract.get, key bounds and InvalidKey (rows
            P12, P15, P16, P20, P21, P23, P28, P44, P45, P47, P50; @plan.Operations.O1, O2, O5, O6). Add an Invariant
            for Reads R8 (P22, P24, both owed checks). The user may split this into its own Task; if so, record it in a
            note.

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Operations.O1, @plan.Operations.O2, @plan.Operations.O5, @plan.Operations.O6.

            - **May change:** `src/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a carry item marked built with no case → caught by the completion
              audit.
            - **Gates:** the suite; falsify.
            - **Stops:** a large public API change.
            - **User's read:** small API calls.
        acceptance
            - The Reads area and every carry item's case pass on production.
            - The Reads features above pass cases on production, and Reads has a Spec section for them.
            - Reads R8 has an Invariant (subscribe starts a request only when missing; no automatic retry).
